<title>BERMUDA: ADT says sees no merit to proposal.</title>
<headline>ADT says sees no merit to proposal.</headline>
<dateline>HAMILTON, Bermuda 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>ADT Ltd said Tuesday it sees no merit in the unsolicited proposals from Western Resources to remove the entire ADT board of directors and replace them with two of Western's employees.</p>
<p>ADT said it is soliciting proxies from its shareholders in opposition to the proposals. The company said it has mailed the proxies relating to the Special General Meeting called for July 8.</p>
<p>ADT said it will, in the near future, be convening a separate meeting to approve certain matters relating to the agreed transaction between itself and Tyco International Ltd.</p>
<p>The company was not immediately able to provide further information.</p>
</text>
